 "_comment": "Dave's edit-copy passes (recovered via pptx_geo_diff.py). Applied by make_brief_slides.py on every rebuild.  TWO THINGS TO KNOW WHEN ADDING ENTRIES.  (1) Keys are the BUILDER's block keys, not the rendered text: a bullet block's key is 'txt:' + the FIRST bullet with its markdown emphasis stripped and NO bullet glyph -- pptx_geo_diff.py prints the rendered form ('• How it reads: ...'), and a key copied from it never matches, so the override is silently dropped (that is what happened to the slide-9 font bump from an earlier pass; fixed 2026-09-18).  (2) An Impress round-trip resizes almost every text block's HEIGHT by a fraction of an inch (autofit recompute: width unchanged, no move).  That is noise and is deliberately NOT recorded here -- only moves, picture geometry, CROPS (cl/cr/ct/cb -- Dave trims figures to fit, and a crop moves nothing, so it was invisible to both diffs until pptx_geo_diff.py learned to report it on 2026-09-18) and font sizes are.  THIRD: an img: key is the figure's BASENAME, so repointing a slide at a newer run silently drops that figure's crop and pinned geometry -- update the key in the same edit (2026-09-18).",
